From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:58:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] horizon on linux: the NVN queue runs on a thread of its own

A submit, a fence and a present are handed to one thread that replays them in order, as a GPU does; the game's thread goes on with the next frame. Syncs are signaled when the queue reaches the fence, a window texture is handed out again only when its last frame was presented, nvnQueueFinish drains. NX2LINUX_NVN_ASYNC=0 replays on the submitting thread. Timing of the draw path (lib draw seconds) added to the log line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: the NVN queue replays on its own thread, as a GPU runs behind the game
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

